    "result_text": "Build passes. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the customerCode de-duplication rule by adding one small, cohesive function rather than growing the existing complex `AssignCustomerCode` (which has a high cyclomatic complexity from its region-mapping cascade).\n\n**New file** \u2014 `DeduplicateCustomerCode.java`: an OfficeFloor step with a single method (CC \u2248 2, WMC_other = 0). It reads the pre-existing owners via `findAll()` (the new owner isn't saved yet at this pipeline stage), and if the computed `customerCode` collides, appends `-<n>` starting at `n=2`, incrementing to the smallest value that is unique.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`: inserted `deduplicateCustomerCode` between `assignCustomerCode` and `assignHousehold`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\nThis keeps structural impact low: no existing function was modified, so every changed/added function has minimal surrounding complexity. The suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test passing \u2014 the `coreCustomerCodesStayUnique` acceptance test asserting distinct owners get distinct codes).",
